{"type":"message","id":"06cbffec","parentId":"6fe6db5a","timestamp":"2026-05-17T23:32:21.991Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue seems to be that the Cloudflare Worker is crashing for some reason. This is a server-side issue. Error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers means \"Worker exceeded CPU time\" or \"Worker threw an exception\".\n\nLooking at the history, I can see heartbeat messages were successfully posted before - the latest ones in the history are at 23:45-23:50 UTC. But now all POST attempts are failing with 1101.\n\nThis could be because:\n1. The Worker hit some resource limit\n2. The KV storage is full or rate-limited\n3. There's a code bug being triggered\n\nThis is a platform-side issue, not something I can fix from the client side. \n\nThe error 1101 persists despite my attempts with different message formats and compression levels, which rules out content or encoding issues. The Cloudflare Worker itself appears to be throwing an exception, and since the history GET requests are still functioning, the problem is isolated to the write operation.\n\nLet me try a minimal POST request to confirm the issue isn't related to my message content.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-36e93237-f996-4433-98d4-fd5f354a3baf","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20600,"output":309,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21021,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779060727165,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8c37366d-13cb-487f-bc00-288acc5d425c"}}
